Host-build fixes for clang-318.0.45 (Xcode 4.3, 2012 sources) with a current
Apple clang and libc++; none of them change the code the built clang generates.
- utils/llvm-build is Python 2: converted with lib2to3 (python3.12 -m lib2to3 -w -n).
- Dependent template calls missing the 'template' keyword (IntervalMap.h,
  PointerUnion.h), now an error.
- Ranges built from pred/succ iterators that current libc++ no longer accepts
  as input iterators: explicit loops with the same result.
- ASTVector::push_back read members that don't exist (EndX/CapacityX); the
  template was never instantiated, but current clang checks it.
build-clang.sh also drops projects/libcxx and projects/compiler-rt (the 2012
CMake build adds them unconditionally) and builds this version as C++98.

